<p>Most of what you set up once lives in <strong>Settings</strong> (the gear in the top bar): your shop's name and time zone, your
  branches and tills, the features you use, and text messages to customers. Shop details, Features and SMS are for the shop's owner;
  owners and managers look after branches and tills.</p>

<%= render "help/walkthrough", tour: HelpTour.find("settings") %>

<h2>Shop details</h2>
<p>Open <strong>Settings › Shop details</strong>. The page is called <strong>Shop settings</strong> and holds:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Business name</strong>: printed on receipts and used in emails and texts.</li>
  <li><strong>Time zone</strong>: sets when your day starts and ends for reports, shifts and the daily email.</li>
  <li><strong>Currency (ISO code)</strong>: three letters, such as KES.</li>
  <li><strong>Largest discount a cashier can give without approval (%)</strong>: see
    <%= link_to "Staff, roles and PINs", help_article_path("staff-and-roles"), class: "link" %>.</li>
  <li><strong>Receipt footer</strong>: a line or two at the bottom of receipts, emailed receipts and invoices, for example your returns
    policy or KRA PIN. The footer is also sent to KRA eTIMS (the first 100 characters).</li>
  <li><strong>Require two-factor sign-in for owners and managers</strong>: once ticked, owners and managers without it are asked to set it
    up the next time they use HardPoint.</li>
</ul>
<p>The page also shows your shop's web address. To change it, contact support. Press <strong>Save settings</strong> when you're done.</p>

<h2>Appearance: your colours and logo</h2>
<p><strong>Settings › Appearance</strong> (owners) chooses the colour of the top bar, buttons and links for everyone at the shop, on
  every screen, the till, the phone and your online store: one of eight themes, or your own brand colour. A colour too light for white
  writing on it is refused, so screens stay readable. Upload your <strong>logo</strong> (PNG or JPEG, under 1 MB) for receipts,
  quotes, invoices, statements and the online store, and choose whether receipts print the <strong>stamp</strong> (the shop, PAID or ON ACCOUNT, the date and branch, in a box).</p>

<h2>Shop preferences</h2>
<p><strong>Settings › Shop preferences</strong> tunes how HardPoint works for you. Anything left alone keeps the usual setting.</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Selling</strong>: how many days a quote is valid (14 to begin with), the payment terms new customers on account get (30
    days), and which payment buttons the till shows. Cash is always there; hide Card, say, if you don't take cards. Also what the till does
    with <strong>stock promised to confirmed orders</strong>: warn the cashier, or hold it for the order (see
    <%= link_to "Customers on account, quotes and orders", help_article_path("customer-accounts"), class: "link" %>).</li>
  <li><strong>Credit control</strong>: put accounts on hold when an invoice is too many days overdue, and remind everyone with an overdue
    invoice each Monday, by SMS or WhatsApp (see <%= link_to "Credit control", help_article_path("credit-control"), class: "link" %>).</li>
  <li><strong>Stock</strong>: how far ahead batches count as expiring (30 days), when stock counts as not selling (90 days, for the dead
    stock report and the Monday email), how many days of sales the reorder list looks at (30), and how long suppliers usually take
    to deliver (7) for those without a lead time of their own.</li>
  <li><strong>Quotes, invoices and statements</strong>: <em>How to pay</em> (your Paybill or bank account) and your <em>Terms</em>,
    printed at the end of each.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Branches</h2>
<p><strong>Settings › Branches</strong> lists your locations. Owners and managers can press <strong>Add branch</strong> and give it a
  <strong>Name</strong>, <strong>Address</strong> and <strong>Phone</strong>. These are printed at the top of its receipts.</p>
<ul>
  <li>Each branch gets a <strong>Receipt code</strong> made from the first letters of its name. Its receipt numbers start with it, for example
    MOI-000123. Press <strong>Edit</strong> to change it: 1 to 6 letters or numbers.</li>
  <li>Each branch has its own tills, stock levels, sales, orders, purchase orders and stock takes. M-Pesa, Airtel Money and KRA eTIMS can be
    set up per branch too.</li>
  <li><strong>Remove branch</strong>, on its edit page, only works for a branch with no tills and no sales.</li>
  <li>How many branches and tills you can have depends on your plan: see
    <%= link_to "Plans, billing and read-only mode", help_article_path("billing"), class: "link" %>.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Tills</h2>
<p><strong>Settings › Tills</strong> lists each point of sale and its branch. Owners and managers press <strong>Add till</strong>, give it a
  name (such as Front counter), pick the branch and choose how receipts print. Untick <strong>In use</strong> to retire a till. Printers and
  cash drawers are explained in
  <%= link_to "Tills, receipt printers, cash drawers and scales", help_article_path("tills-and-printers"), class: "link" %>.</p>

<h2>Features</h2>
<p><strong>Settings › Features</strong> switches parts of HardPoint on and off: deliveries, promotions, foreign currencies, the online store,
  WhatsApp from HardPoint, the customer portal, fundi commissions, contractor jobs, batches and expiry dates, serial numbers, and the API. Press <strong>Save features</strong> after changing them. See
  <%= link_to "Switching features on and off", help_article_path("getting-around", anchor: "features"), class: "link" %>.</p>

<h2>Text messages (SMS)</h2>
<p>HardPoint can text customers through Africa's Talking. To turn it on:</p>
<ol>
  <li>Open <strong>Settings › SMS</strong>. It takes you to the bottom of Shop details.</li>
  <li>Tick <strong>Send texts to customers (SMS)</strong> and press <strong>Save settings</strong>.</li>
</ol>
<p>Once it's on:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Receipts</strong>: after a sale, type the customer's number in <strong>Text receipt to…</strong> and press <strong>Text</strong>.
    On a past sale, use <strong>Text the receipt</strong>.</li>
  <li><strong>Order ready</strong>: on a customer order, <strong>Mark ready and text</strong> (with the customer's first name) tells them to
    come and collect, with anything left to pay. The customer needs a phone number.</li>
  <li><strong>Balance reminders</strong>: on a customer who owes money, <strong>Text a reminder</strong> sends their balance, what's overdue,
    and your Paybill if you have one. Owners, managers and accountants can send these, once a day per customer. Nothing is texted to a
    customer with <strong>Don't text this customer</strong> ticked.</li>
  <li><strong>Online orders</strong>: customers who order from your online store get a text saying you have their order.</li>
</ul>
<p>Texts only go to Kenyan mobile numbers. A shop can send up to 500 texts a day, so a mistake can't run up a bill.</p>

<h2>Seeing what was sent</h2>
<p>Under the SMS tick box, Shop details shows how many texts went this month and a <strong>Texts sent</strong> link. That page lists each
  text: when, to whom, what kind, the message, who sent it and whether it was <strong>Sent</strong> or <strong>Failed</strong>, with
  its cost where Africa's Talking reported one.</p>

<h2>Elsewhere in Settings</h2>
<p>Staff and activity are in <%= link_to "Staff, roles and PINs", help_article_path("staff-and-roles"), class: "link" %>. Payments and tax have
  their own guides: <%= link_to "M-Pesa payments", help_article_path("mpesa"), class: "link" %>,
  <%= link_to "Airtel Money", help_article_path("airtel-money"), class: "link" %> and
  <%= link_to "KRA eTIMS", help_article_path("etims"), class: "link" %>. Exporting and closing the account are in
  <%= link_to "Exporting your data and closing your account", help_article_path("your-data"), class: "link" %>.</p>
